1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,944
Here is a simple way to make a better short video.

2
00:00:02,944 --> 00:00:04,533
Start with one useful idea.

3
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:05,416
Not five ideas.

4
00:00:05,416 --> 00:00:07,830
Just one thing your viewer can use today.

5
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:09,937
The first sentence matters.

6
00:00:09,937 --> 00:00:11,901
Tell people what they will learn.

7
00:00:11,901 --> 00:00:12,794
Then show them.

8
00:00:12,794 --> 00:00:15,830
A clear example is better than a long introduction.

9
00:00:16,330 --> 00:00:18,764
Keep the parts that move the story forward.

10
00:00:18,764 --> 00:00:20,520
Leave a little room to breathe.

11
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:23,690
Captions help people follow along when the sound is off.

12
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:27,111
Before you export, watch it once on a small screen.

13
00:00:27,111 --> 00:00:32,265
Can you read the words? Is the subject in frame? Does the ending give people a next step?.

14
00:00:32,765 --> 00:00:36,249
You do not need a perfect setup to make something useful.

15
00:00:36,249 --> 00:00:40,100
Record an idea, make a thoughtful cut, and share what you know.